WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:01.730
"It's too dangerous.

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.950
I have to go alone."

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:07.121
Those are the words Daisy Ridley's Rey utters
in the brand-new footage from Star Wars: The

00:00:07.121 --> 00:00:10.890
Rise of Skywalker shown at 2019's D23 Expo.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.880
Lucasfilm took the stage on Saturday during
the hotly anticipated Walt Disney Studios

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.009
presentation to unveil fresh footage from
the Star Wars saga-ending The Rise of Skywalker.

00:00:20.009 --> 00:00:23.949
Director J.J. Abrams explained that the creative
team is working hard on putting the finishing

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:27.820
touches on the film and is tinkering away
at a new trailer to reveal ahead of the movie's

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.699
December 20 release date.

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:32.500
But he didn't want to leave the Star Wars
fans in attendance hanging.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.950
So, he, his Lucasfilm partners, and The Rise
of Skywalker cast gifted the world with a

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.520
stellar sizzle reel featuring shots from the
flick.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.990
The footage reportedly received a standing
ovation.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:45.970
The Hollywood Reporter had the breakdown of
the footage, which shows a sizable fleet of

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:50.190
Star Destroyers clustered in the sky, Rey
and Kylo Ren battling atop a sunken ship in

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.300
the ocean, and a first look at Keri Russell's
character Zorri Bliss in action — a Boba

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.460
Fett-style bounty hunter type whom Russell
describes as, quote, "very cool and a little

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.050
bit shady … kind of a criminal."

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.760
She's also apparently an old friend of Poe
Dameron's.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.900
The new Rise of Skywalker footage ended with
the most jaw-dropping shot of all: Rey is

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.560
seen cloaked in a dark hood and holding a
dual-bladed lightsaber that's glowing red.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.920
"That lightsaber… it belongs to me."

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.360
This suggests that Rey, who struggled with
understanding and channeling the Force in

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.720
The Last Jedi, may give into temptation and
turn to the dark side in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.750
C'mon, a red saber with two blades?

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.620
A black hood over her head?

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.920
Rey's giving serious dark side vibes in the
new footage, and it's already sending fans

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.630
into a spiral of speculation - with many theorizing
that the get-up she sports in the new footage

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.530
may be her response to discovering her true
parentage, which has always been a hot point

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.880
of discussion amongst fans.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.080
If The Rise of Skywalker reveals that Rey
is a descendant of a prominent dark-sider

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.400
- like, say, Emperor Palpatine - she certainly
couldn't be blamed for having an existential

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.400
crisis.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.710
On the other hand, maybe she's wearing a creepy
hood and wielding a new lightsaber because

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.400
she's trying to infiltrate the First Order
as part of a Resistance mission.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.280
That seems more likely than Rey going mad,
but hey, anything goes in the Star Wars universe.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.000
Unfortunately, The Rise of Skywalker sizzle
reel wasn't immediately made available online.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.580
The silver lining is that something else related
to the movie is: a badass new poster.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.890
Lucasfilm unveiled the one-sheet at the Walt
Disney Studios presentation on Saturday, giving

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.940
fans a glimpse at the tone and aesthetic of
the upcoming film.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:24.440
Aside from Palpatine's tell-tale cackle in
the first Rise of Skywalker teaser, It's one

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.690
of the first confirmations that the one-time
Emperor of the galaxy will be playing a role

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:29.690
in Episode 9.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:33.360
These reveals should tide fans over until
Lucasfilm drops the second trailer for The

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.600
Rise of Skywalker, and definitely serve to
boost hype for the flick that will supposedly

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.090
cap off the nine-movie Skywalker saga.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.250
The Star Wars franchise will, of course, live
on after The Rise of Skywalker with new movies

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.870
from Last Jedi director Rian Johnson, and
Game of Thrones creators David Benioff and

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.870
D.B. Weiss.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.069
There's also the three live-action Star Wars
TV series coming to the Disney+ streaming

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:59.239
platform: The Mandalorian, a Rogue One prequel
centered on Diego Luna's character Cassian

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:02.180
Andor, and the recently announced Obi-Wan
Kenobi show.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.180
"Hello there."

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.379
Still, The Rise of Skywalker marks the end
of an important era, and will apparently be

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:11.490
the last Star Wars film for a while, as the
franchise is taking a hiatus from feature

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.970
films after its release.

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:17.050
The hope is that The Rise of Skywalker will
be so epic that fans completely forget there

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.160
won't be a new Star Wars movie hitting the
big screen for some time.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.440
Based on this footage description, the new
poster, and the action-packed first trailer,

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.240
that goal should be easily achieved.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.709
The end is nigh, and the saga is sure to go
out with a bang when Episode 9 lands in theaters

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:31.870
on December 20.

